  "project": "madelon-reanalysis",
  "reason": "What the two trails of 15 November reached, from project.py propose. Both trails reproduced the inherited cross-validated AUC and saw it miss the held-out floor (live-1 step-8, live-2 step-7: the same command on the same code tree and data), and both measured an estimate that agrees once selection is inside cross-validation (live-1 step-13 with diagnose.py, live-2 step-11). The floor was cleared twice, by different methods: live-1 step-18 with L1-penalised logistic regression, live-2 step-19 with a random forest. Each of those observations also meets the other floor node's criteria, since the criteria are the same; the plans that each trail ran say which method it was, so live-1 resolves floor-l1 only and live-2 floor-forest only. The goals explain and floor are reached. compact is open, and its three routes all pass screen next.",
